{"availability":"available","full":"camusdb/camusdb","name":"camusdb","description":"CamusDB is a SQL distributed database written in C# on .NET. It pairs a SQL interface with a Raft-replicated, transactional k/v storage layer, it makes opinionated choices: serializable isolation/strong consistency by default, databases can be branched copy-on-write and it can auto-scale to adapt to traffic","category":"Developer tools","language":"C#","stars":15,"forks":1,"created":"2021-11-28T09:12:12Z","updated":"2026-10-10T16:39:34Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://camusdb.github.io/","topics":["c-sharp","camusdb","consistency","database","distributed","distributed-sql-database","dotnet","kv","persistence","raft","serializable","sql"],"demo":"https://camusdb.github.io/playground/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:26.340Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:26.340Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:26.340Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:54:23.944Z","stars":13,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-09T08:56:15.735Z","stars":14,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-10T21:05:26.340Z","stars":15,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["CamusDB is a SQL distributed database written in C# on .NET. It provides a SQL interface with a Raft-replicated, transactional key-value storage layer, and makes a few opinionated choices: serializable isolation/strong consistency are the default; databases can be branched copy-on-write like code; and dropped objects are recoverable instead of instantly destroyed. It can auto-scale based on traffic. Development is driven by performance, Jepsen-style testing, chaos engineering, fault injection, and degraded-state testing.","While CamusDB is actively used in production, some of its features are considered alpha, use it with caution. APIs and storage formats may change between versions."],"features":["SQL dialect — SELECT (including FROM-less SELECT ), INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, TRUNCATE, CREATE/DROP/ALTER TABLE, transactions (BEGIN / COMMIT / ROLLBACK), parameterized placeholders, prepared statements, table aliases,…","ACID transactions — pessimistic locking by default, with optimistic locking per transaction (SET TRANSACTION LOCKING OPTIMISTIC); serializable isolation is the default (range/predicate locks with wait-die deadlock…","Copy-on-write database branching — fork a database instantly with CREATE DATABASE featurex BRANCH FROM prod; inspect the tree with SHOW BRANCHES FROM db and SHOW ANCESTORS FROM db.","Recovering dropped objects — deferred physical deletion with RELINK TO '' recovery, SHOW ORPHAN DATABASES / SHOW ORPHAN TABLES, and a background reclaimer.","Time-travel reads — SELECT … AS OF SYSTEM TIME '-10s' (or an absolute UTC timestamp / epoch ms) runs the whole statement against a consistent historical snapshot; lock-free, never blocks writers, usable to read back…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/camusdb/camusdb/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ffc96ebd06d89f5a9e0da057a65f3e7e6919d889929c859da33648f57d75ac76","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:26.677Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:26.677Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"CamusDB is a SQL distributed database written in C# on .NET. It provides a SQL interface with a Raft-replicated, transactional key-value storage layer, and makes a few opinionated choices: serializable isolation/strong consistency are the default; databases can be branched copy-on-write like code; and dropped objects are recoverable instead of instantly destroyed. It can auto-scale based on traffic. Development is driven by performance, Jepsen-style testing, chaos engineering, fault injection, and degraded-state testing.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/camusdb/camusdb/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"ffc96ebd06d89f5a9e0da057a65f3e7e6919d889929c859da33648f57d75ac76","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/camusdb/camusdb/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt